 Consumer errors retain their full evidence. Resume successful completed archive
 only after all saved hashes and bindings revalidate; partial unmarked CPU archive
 fails closed for manual inspection. Root alone handles GPU/service lifecycle.
+
+Version 2 administrative recovery (2026-10-17)
+The producer may finalize only after a successful immutable run archive. The receiver still checks every original archive SHA and every producer SHA. The sole exception is queue.finalize changing boolean false to boolean true; the entire other queue object must remain equal. A root_release_request must identify the exact pinned service PID/identity, exact successful current-run RUN_GATE path and SHA, and a release time no earlier than that gate. The original queue/inventory/gate are preserved. Any other mutation fails closed.
+B51317 already completed pose and all186 scan rows before this administrative final check. RECOVERY_BINDING fixes those existing output hashes before explicit recovery. Recovery verifies actual video/frame/model/code/source/scan bindings and does not execute pose/scan/model. Recorded elapsed time is the sum of original integrity, pose and scan durations (not reconstructed wall); recovery verification cost is separately recorded. Partial archives otherwise remain fail-closed.
+The consumer v1 failure and all version1 files remain in versions/v1_before_finalize_recovery. No producer/runtime files are modified by this change.
